5
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,980
But where is it coming from?

6
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:09,860
There's no person typing.

7
00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:11,860
It isn't copying a webpage.

8
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:14,359
Most of the time, it isn't

9
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,580
looking anything up at all.

10
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:17,779
So where does the answer come

11
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:18,060
from?

12
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:20,520
Let's un-jargon it.

13
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:21,800
Quick test.

14
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:24,559
Finish this sentence Once upon

15
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:24,880
a…

16
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,540
You said time, didn't you?

17
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:30,692
then you just did exactly what

18
00:00:30,693 --> 00:00:31,853
ChatGPT does.

19
00:00:32,993 --> 00:00:34,873
ChatGPT is a guessing machine.

20
00:00:35,413 --> 00:00:37,312
It looks at the word so far and

21
00:00:37,313 --> 00:00:38,832
guesses the most likely next

22
00:00:38,833 --> 00:00:39,093
word.

23
00:00:39,653 --> 00:00:41,493
It adds that word, looks again,

24
00:00:41,753 --> 00:00:43,672
and guesses the next one, and

25
00:00:43,673 --> 00:00:44,093
the next.

26
00:00:45,173 --> 00:00:45,853
That's it.

27
00:00:46,573 --> 00:00:47,972
Every answer it has ever given

28
00:00:47,973 --> 00:00:49,752
you was built like that, one

29
00:00:49,753 --> 00:00:50,613
guess at a time.

30
00:00:51,553 --> 00:00:52,593
So three questions.

31
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:54,213
Guessing from what?

32
00:00:54,853 --> 00:00:56,052
Why can't it count letters?

33
00:00:56,053 --> 00:00:58,172
And why does the same question

34
00:00:58,173 --> 00:00:59,173
get different answers?

35
00:00:59,933 --> 00:01:01,472
Question one, guessing from

36
00:01:01,473 --> 00:01:01,753
what?

37
00:01:02,373 --> 00:01:03,992
You knew time because you've

38
00:01:03,993 --> 00:01:05,553
heard that line 100 times.

39
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:08,053
ChatGPT learned the same way,

40
00:01:08,353 --> 00:01:09,613
just on a giant scale.

41
00:01:10,693 --> 00:01:11,732
Remember, fill in the blank

42
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:12,793
worksheets from school.

43
00:01:13,493 --> 00:01:14,513
The cat sat on the blank.

44
00:01:15,233 --> 00:01:15,993
That's its training.

45
00:01:16,693 --> 00:01:18,213
It was shown a mountain of text,

46
00:01:18,533 --> 00:01:20,572
books, websites, articles, with

47
00:01:20,573 --> 00:01:21,493
the next word hidden.

48
00:01:22,073 --> 00:01:22,553
It guessed.

49
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:24,213
The guess was checked.

50
00:01:24,853 --> 00:01:26,532
If it was wrong, it got adjusted

51
00:01:26,533 --> 00:01:27,333
a tiny bit.

52
00:01:27,863 --> 00:01:30,193
Then again, billions of times.

53
00:01:31,233 --> 00:01:32,753
Nobody gave it a list of facts.

54
00:01:33,393 --> 00:01:34,912
It just got incredibly good at

55
00:01:34,913 --> 00:01:35,233
blanks.

56
00:01:35,893 --> 00:01:37,652
That's why this kind of AI is

57
00:01:37,653 --> 00:01:38,773
called a language model.

58
00:01:39,433 --> 00:01:40,872
Then people trained it some more

59
00:01:40,873 --> 00:01:42,112
to answer like a helpful

60
00:01:42,113 --> 00:01:42,573
assistant.

61
00:01:43,233 --> 00:01:44,852
But underneath, it's still the

62
00:01:44,853 --> 00:01:46,192
world's best fill in the blank

63
00:01:46,193 --> 00:01:46,493
player.

64
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:49,479
Question two, how many R's are

65
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,020
in strawberry?

66
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:53,520
Three, but for a long time,

67
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:55,659
ChatGPT would confidently say

68
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:56,340
two.

69
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:58,060
Here's why.

70
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,079
I've been saying it guesses the

71
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:00,660
next word.

72
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:02,540
That was a little white lie.

73
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:04,800
It doesn't see words or letters.

74
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:06,980
It sees chunks called tokens.

75
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,279
Your message gets chopped into

76
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:11,459
pieces and each piece becomes a

77
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:11,680
number.

78
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:13,879
Strawberry might get chopped

79
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,380
into three pieces like this.

80
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:17,879
Now imagine I text you a

81
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:19,939
strawberry emoji and ask how

82
00:02:19,940 --> 00:02:21,040
